{
  "requirement": "Ordinary evidence validation, status inspection, and book rendering MUST continue\nto check evidence using the existing rules without invoking models, contacting\nproviders, or requiring authoring configuration or credentials. Missing or stale\nevidence MUST remain a validation failure rather than trigger authoring.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met.** The code marked {impl} covers each obligation, and the tests cover the main cases. The one weakness is that a few of the {test} anchors are broader than the behaviour they exercise.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` `fn[main]` loads only the workspace evidence settings for commands other than `author`. `status`, `info`, `setup`, `hook` and `mdbook supports` skip even that. Only `author` reaches `config::resolve_authoring` (via `authoring/batch.rs` and `authoring/mod.rs`) and the provider code. `status`, `info` and `mdbook` (book rendering) therefore never read the user authoring configuration or credentials, never invoke a model, and never contact a provider.\n- `src/config.rs` `fn[load_workspace_evidence]` decodes and validates only `[evidence]` and the common workspace structure. It does not decode `[authoring]`. It only checks whether `authoring.configs.*` contains credential keys, so unused or invalid authoring settings cannot fail ordinary validation.\n- `src/evidence.rs` `fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]` is the shared validation path. It reports missing evidence as an error string (\"missing for …\") and does not start authoring. Stale evidence is reported by `validate_evidence_file`. This keeps the existing rules and the failure behaviour the requirement asks for.\n- I found no {impl} anchors that carry behaviour outside this requirement. The other requirements anchored on these functions are listed separately. I also found no unmarked code that implements part of this requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` `missing_or_stale_evidence_fails_validation_without_contacting_the_provider` covers the main points.\n  - It runs both the missing and the stale case.\n  - It calls `validate_repository` and expects an error that names the subject.\n  - It runs `status` with the credential env var removed, and it runs the `mdbook` preprocessor, also with the credential removed. Both succeed.\n  - It binds a listener as the provider endpoint and asserts that no connection arrived.\n  - It asserts that no usage state was written and that the evidence file was not rewritten.\n- `ordinary_status_ignores_invalid_user_authoring_configuration` writes a malformed user config. `status` still succeeds, no authoring state is created, and the evidence file is unchanged.\n- `tests/commands.rs` `status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring` and `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs` `validation_checks_workspace_common_config_without_loading_unused_authoring_settings` cover the workspace file. An invalid `[authoring]` section is ignored, while invalid common structure or `[evidence]` settings are still reported as findings.\n- `status_applies_workspace_disallow_to_existing_evidence` shows the existing validation rules still apply.\n- The {test} anchor on `Fixture::run` is a helper annotation and adds no coverage of its own.\n- I judge the coverage sufficient: it includes the failure cases (missing, stale, invalid configuration) and the negative checks (no provider contact, no authoring writes).\n\nNo FIXME or acknowledged gaps were found.",
